{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"]}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"generated":true,"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"targets SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}]},{"text":" — computed properties, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-four-rules","type":"heading","text":"The four rules"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gesture + "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"@GestureState","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"origami.drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — Drag"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" + update logic"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(.spring)"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"code":"View","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" body. Origami "},{"code":"Transition","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s "},{"code":".transition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier — that’s a different concept)."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","type":"heading","text":"Pure value patch → computed property"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition\/interpolate"},{"type":"text","text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property (or an inline expression) — no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", no side effect."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","type":"heading","text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"down"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDoubleTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onLongPress"},{"type":"text","text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose output lands in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture arbitration clean."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","type":"heading","text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", and other animation patches drive a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier on the animated property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","text":"Flag, don’t fake","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute-position layout."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","title":"Swami","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swami","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Beats","abstract":[{"text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text"